1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,115
Small print, repeated facts, and too much typing can make paperwork exhausting. Unbound Access takes one question at a time.

2
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:15,890
Large controls and read aloud support spoken or typed answers. The person reviews every change and keeps control of the record.

3
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:24,870
This edited walkthrough uses actual app screens, fictional typed data, and generic synthetic narration. It is not continuous voice capture.

4
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:32,265
An answer is only a proposal. Cancel leaves saved answers unchanged. Confirm moves to the next question.

5
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:38,960
The prepared form says household size must be one through twelve. Thirteen is rejected before it can be saved.

6
00:00:39,280 --> 00:00:46,655
Two is accepted. Zero dollars is also a valid income answer, rather than being mistaken for a missing value.

7
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:54,140
Answer Yes to access support and the required follow up appears. Here the fictional request is questions read aloud.

8
00:00:54,440 --> 00:01:01,715
Now correct the home address from forty to forty one Practice Street. The app shows both linked fields and their previous values.

9
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:10,630
Confirmation updates both home answers together. The separate landlord address stays ninety Venue Lane. Shared facts do not cross different people.

10
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:18,765
Review the source linked answers, acknowledge the review, and download the PDF. Persistent Save and Open links allow another attempt.

11
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:26,385
These are both pages of the actual browser downloaded file. The corrected addresses and zero income survived export and were checked.

12
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:33,205
This is a readable answer record, not a filled original agency form. Nothing is signed or submitted.

13
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:42,450
Built with Llama. Optional Meta Llama three point two, one billion parameters, runs genuine inference inside the browser through w llama.

14
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:52,070
The revised development run correctly interpreted three clear answers: three people, zero dollars, and No. Its unchanged raw outputs are preserved.

15
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:59,260
It also guessed three when the input was uncertain. The current source guard rejects that guess. This is not a model success.

16
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:10,515
Question extraction failed required flag validation. General extraction remains experimental and unreliable. Prepared forms and direct controls remain available.

17
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:19,745
The optional model download is about eight hundred eight megabytes, with explicit consent and removal controls. CPU inference is slow.

18
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:28,335
No API key, card, or paid fallback is needed. Local model tasks stay in the browser; browser speech may use a remote service.

19
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:36,930
Eighty six automated checks passed. The complete typed browser journey and downloaded PDF were verified separately from model quality.

20
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:47,735
One tester reported phone audio, microphone, and sample PDF opening. Full phone dictation, timed usability, and GPU offload remain unverified.

21
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:56,105
Try the working form, inspect real inference receipts, and read the public source. Every confirmed answer remains yours to review.

